(921,1922,'Perception of painful and nonpainful phantom sensations that occur following the complete or partial loss of a limb. The majority of individuals with an amputated extremity will experience the impression that the limb is still present, and in many cases, painful. (From Neurol Clin 1998 Nov;16(4):919-36; Brain 1998 Sep;121(Pt 9):1603-30)','en',2,'2026-08-11 20:23:27',NULL,NULL,'9203FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
